## Model card

- **Name:** Grok 5
- **Short description:** xAI's next-generation flagship language model, currently in training on the Colossus 2 supercluster and not yet released. Distinct from the shipped Grok 4.5/4.6/4.7 flagships (which grew out of the ~1.5T-parameter V9-Medium coding foundation) and from Grok 4.20's multi-agent beta build.
- **Provider / access:** none available — no API endpoint, no consumer app listing. xAI's official model docs (`docs.x.ai/docs/models`) list grok-4.7 as the most capable text model and contain no `grok-5` entry (verified 2026-10-09).
- **Release / knowledge:** not released as of 2026-10-09. Confirmed to exist and be training in xAI's January 2026 funding announcement ($20B Series E, ~$230B valuation). Musk's earlier targets (late 2025, Q1 2026, Q2 2026) all passed with no launch; his September 14, 2026 roadmap places Grok 4.8 and 4.9 ahead of Grok 5. Polymarket priced a 2026 launch near a coin flip in mid-September 2026.
- **IDs:** no provider/model-id exists (no Free ID anywhere; model unreleased)
- **Context window:** no official figure. The widely repeated ~1.5M-token estimate is unconfirmed; shipping xAI models list 500K (grok-4.5/4.6/4.7), 1M (grok-4.3/4.20), 256K (grok-build-0.1).
- **Modalities:** expected native multimodal and live X data, but nothing is specified for Grok 5; no verified specification.
- **Pricing (as of 2026-10-09):** unannounced. Only the current xAI ladder is known: grok-4.7 at $2/$6 per 1M tokens ($4/$12 at ≥200K prompt tokens), grok-4.3 at $1.25/$2.50.
- **Architecture:** rumored 6T–10T total parameters, mixture-of-experts, trained on Colossus 2 (~550K NVIDIA GB200/GB300 GPUs; seven models training simultaneously at 1T/1.5T/6T/10T scales). No model card confirms any number. "AGI" claims are Musk self-stated predictions ("10% and rising", October 2025; "That will be Grok 5", September 14, 2026), not measurements.

